analyzer.1:
Return strict JSON only: {{"accepted": true_or_false, "clue_type": "...", "rarity_category": "common_or_rare", "reasoning_steps_valid": true_or_false, "shape_independent": true_or_false, "notes": [strings]}}.
Target={color}; requested_entropy_bin={bin_id}; candidate={candidate_json}
Validate the semantic contract; do not trust the candidate's self-reported fields.
Bin 1 standard: strongly directed, one-step inference, no color term;
single objects or short enumerations of 2-4 everyday objects are both fine
as long as EVERY listed object's dominant color is factually the target
(reject if a central part of any object has a different dominant color);
reject if another color is an equally natural answer or the clue names any
color.
